# Caddy as an existing reverse proxy (PROXY_MODE=external), for a Caddy you already run for other sites.
# Without one, prefer PROXY_MODE=bundled: the stack brings its own Caddy (deploy/caddy/Caddyfile).
#
# Prerequisite: server:3000 and livekit:7880 are reachable for Caddy.
#   - Caddy on the host:    docker compose --env-file ../.env -f compose.yml -f proxies/nginx.ports.yml --profile external up -d
#                           (publishes both ports only on 127.0.0.1)
#   - Caddy in a container: attach it to the network "squorli_internal" and below
#                           replace 127.0.0.1:3000 -> server:3000, 127.0.0.1:7880 -> livekit:7880.
# Copy the site block into your Caddyfile, replace chat.example.org, `caddy reload`. Caddy gets the certificate itself,
# redirects HTTP to HTTPS, passes WebSocket upgrades and sets X-Forwarded-For/-Proto; no body size limit by default.
#
# Not through Caddy: 7881/tcp and 7882/udp (media) must pass directly to the host (firewall).
# Subdomain only, no subpath. Tested by deploy/proxies/test/run.sh (docs/features/proxy-tests.md).

chat.example.org {
	# LiveKit signaling (WebSocket under /rtc, validation under /rtc/validate)
	reverse_proxy /rtc* 127.0.0.1:7880

	# App server: API, WebSocket /api/ws, static web client
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
}
